// E0012: a `/*` block comment with no closing `*/` runs to end-of-file. It
// used to silently swallow the rest of the file (including `main`) while the
// compiler still reported "No errors found" (exit 0) — a valid-looking build
// of a file that never compiled. The lexer now emits a diagnostic, matching
// the unterminated-string / unterminated-char handling.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0012)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::UnterminatedBlockComment;

function main() -> int {
    return 0;
}

/* this block comment is intentionally never closed
